# Networking task

Task: Using nftables, drop all incoming IPv4 traffic whose source address belongs to the network `{{blocked_subnet}}`. The rule must be active in the running ruleset, must be loaded automatically at boot through the nftables service, and its configuration must live in `/etc/nftables.conf` or in a file included from it.

Do not add any rule that blocks or restricts SSH access on port 22 from other networks, and do not change the policy of existing chains to drop.
